From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fixture Developer <dev@mobimanual.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Wi-Fi policies

A Wi-Fi policy puts a company network on the devices of its groups: the
network name (SSID), the security type and the password. The security type
is WPA2 Personal, WPA3 Personal or WPA2 Enterprise; Enterprise asks for a
user name instead of a shared password and uses the device owner's
directory account.

It is a fourth policy type next to Passcode, Kiosk and Restrictions, with
its own page under Policies, and is assigned to groups like the others.
---
Expected: worth documenting, and partly beyond what DocBot can write. Triage answers doc-impact. The draft corrects "There are three types: Passcode, Kiosk and Restrictions" on _policies.md, and says in uncertainties that the manual has no page for Wi-Fi policies (_policies_wifi.md, which a human has to write and add to htmlDocPages). Writing the Wi-Fi settings into an existing page as a stand-in for the missing one is wrong.
Expected-outcome: opened
Expected-edits: _policies.md

